    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ec2ed94b0dfb5c55b428507ec850f7342db40e8f508969c29e014891206811aa",
      "text": "After a morning walk in the forest, you'll leave the Saramacca River area for Peperpot Nature Park, one of Suriname's well-known birdwatching areas.\n\nA large plantation once stood here. Tropical forest gradually grew around its old canals, avenues and service buildings. Today, the traces of plantation life and the wild forest sit side by side in a small area.\n\nTowards evening, you'll check in at a boutique hotel near the park. You'll take another walk after dusk. In the dark, it pays to listen. You often hear the birds before you catch sight of them.\n\nIncluded today: transfers, guide services and hotel accommodation.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-6f717a3eb013fcd209dd952042ffc350",
        "model": "GPT-6.1",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The Word Day 4 itinerary has the same transfer and evening walk but no corresponding account of the canals, avenues and service buildings or of locating birds by sound."
      }
    },
